test_custom_scan
================

A custom scan provider for tests. It wraps every subquery in FROM whose
alias is "cscan" in a custom scan that passes the rows of its children
through: the subquery's plan is its one child, or each branch of a
UNION ALL is a child. A test can so put any plan under a custom scan,
such as a Motion, a shared scan of a CTE or a SubPlan, and check that
the planner, the dispatcher and the executor reach the custom scan's
children as they reach those of any other plan node.

The plan of a query with the scan reaches the segments, so the library
must be loaded in every backend of the cluster. The setup test adds it
to session_preload_libraries with gpconfig and reloads the cluster; the
teardown test removes it. Run the tests against a running cluster:

    make install
    make installcheck
